{"journal_version":1,"sequence":5,"replace_from":2,"message_count":3,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"We need answer verdict. Need review. Need inspect mentally. Key issue: acceptance says At /?sync=error, retry immediately returns to Checking service…, then completes as \"All changes are synced.\" after same simulated delay. Existing effect reads requested = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('sync')? Need see omitted lines. Diff shows effect callback sets requested === 'error' ? error : success. On retry at /?sync=error, attempt increment reruns effect, requested still error, so after 120ms it returns to error, not success. Developer report acknowledges this: \"Retry always re-reads ?sync=error ... land back on error state after delay (as required by 'same simulated delay' wording); success transition covered by existing success path.\" But acceptance explicitly: \"Activating it immediately returns the panel to Checking service…, then completes as All changes are synced. after the same simulated delay.\" This is unmet. Concrete FAIL. Need name severity, affected behavior, exact diff evidence, repro, bounded fix. Also maybe overlapping timers? Effect cleanup prevents overlap; okay. Need mention success path never retry; yes. Retry button in error branch. The primary bug: retry re-runs effect that re-reads URL in error. Need fix decouple initial URL condition from retry so retry forces success. E.g., use a query param only once or a ref/state indicating retry; effect: const requested = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('sync'); setState(attempt > 0 ? 'success' : requested === 'error' ? 'error' : 'success'); Or store initial requested in ref and retry flag. Must preserve immediate loading, no overlapping timers. Could also ensure retry button not repeated activation? When clicked set loading, button disappears immediately so no repeated? In React batched state, second click before rerender? Button may remain until render, but handleRetry both setState loading and attempt increment; repeated activation increments attempts, effect cleanup clears timers, no overlap. Fine.\n\nNeed final first line exactly VERDICT: FAIL. Concise within token. No tools. Ensure no extra first line. Include severity, behavior, evidence, repro, fix. Maybe mention acceptance criterion. We can include only one finding. Need say public tests maybe didn't cover. Good.","content":"VERDICT: FAIL\n\n**Finding — High severity: Retry returns to error instead of success at `/?sync=error`.**\n\nAffected behavior: The acceptance criterion requires retry to show `Checking service…` immediately and then complete as `All changes are synced.` after the simulated delay. The diff instead re-runs the same effect, which re-reads `?sync=error`, so after 120 ms it sets state back to `'error'`.\n\nExact diff evidence:\n```tsx\nconst requested = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('sync');\n...\nsetState(requested === 'error' ? 'error' : 'success');\n...\n}, [attempt]);\n\nfunction handleRetry() {\n  setState('loading');\n  setAttempt((current) => current + 1);\n}\n```\n\nBecause `attempt` only re-triggers the existing effect and the URL still contains `sync=error`, retry deterministically returns to `Sync failed`.\n\nReproduction:\n1. Open `/?sync=error`.\n2. Confirm the error state and `Retry sync`.\n3. Activate `Retry sync`.\n4. Observe `Checking service…` immediately.\n5. After the simulated delay, observe `Sync failed` again instead of `All changes are synced.`\n\nBounded fix: Make retry force the success result while preserving the initial URL-driven error state. For example, track whether this run is a retry and set the result accordingly:\n```tsx\nconst isRetry = attempt > 0;\n...\nsetState(isRetry || requested !== 'error' ? 'success' : 'error');\n```\nor store the initial query result in a ref and let `handleRetry()` trigger a success attempt. Keep the existing effect cleanup so timers remain non-overlapping.","response_items":[{"id":"3176768a-29aa-4154-a6c5-f21ec8116e2a","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need answer verdict. Need review. Need inspect mentally. Key issue: acceptance says At /?sync=error, retry immediately returns to Checking service…, then completes as \"All changes are synced.\" after same simulated delay. Existing effect reads requested = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('sync')? Need see omitted lines. Diff shows effect callback sets requested === 'error' ? error : success. On retry at /?sync=error, attempt increment reruns effect, requested still error, so after 120ms it returns to error, not success. Developer report acknowledges this: \"Retry always re-reads ?sync=error ... land back on error state after delay (as required by 'same simulated delay' wording); success transition covered by existing success path.\" But acceptance explicitly: \"Activating it immediately returns the panel to Checking service…, then completes as All changes are synced. after the same simulated delay.\" This is unmet. Concrete FAIL. Need name severity, affected behavior, exact diff evidence, repro, bounded fix. Also maybe overlapping timers? Effect cleanup prevents overlap; okay. Need mention success path never retry; yes. Retry button in error branch. The primary bug: retry re-runs effect that re-reads URL in error. Need fix decouple initial URL condition from retry so retry forces success. E.g., use a query param only once or a ref/state indicating retry; effect: const requested = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('sync'); setState(attempt > 0 ? 'success' : requested === 'error' ? 'error' : 'success'); Or store initial requested in ref and retry flag. Must preserve immediate loading, no overlapping timers. Could also ensure retry button not repeated activation? When clicked set loading, button disappears immediately so no repeated? In React batched state, second click before rerender? Button may remain until render, but handleRetry both setState loading and attempt increment; repeated activation increments attempts, effect cleanup clears timers, no overlap. Fine.\n\nNeed final first line exactly VERDICT: FAIL. Concise within token. No tools. Ensure no extra first line. Include severity, behavior, evidence, repro, fix. Maybe mention acceptance criterion. We can include only one finding. Need say public tests maybe didn't cover. Good.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":"30dae7b5-bc8c-4878-a9c2-8d77122242af-0","status":"completed"},{"id":"487bdade-18c9-4397-8864-b24e2c288cf2","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"VERDICT: FAIL\n\n**Finding — High severity: Retry returns to error instead of success at `/?sync=error`.**\n\nAffected behavior: The acceptance criterion requires retry to show `Checking service…` immediately and then complete as `All changes are synced.` after the simulated delay. The diff instead re-runs the same effect, which re-reads `?sync=error`, so after 120 ms it sets state back to `'error'`.\n\nExact diff evidence:\n```tsx\nconst requested = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('sync');\n...\nsetState(requested === 'error' ? 'error' : 'success');\n...\n}, [attempt]);\n\nfunction handleRetry() {\n  setState('loading');\n  setAttempt((current) => current + 1);\n}\n```\n\nBecause `attempt` only re-triggers the existing effect and the URL still contains `sync=error`, retry deterministically returns to `Sync failed`.\n\nReproduction:\n1. Open `/?sync=error`.\n2. Confirm the error state and `Retry sync`.\n3. Activate `Retry sync`.\n4. Observe `Checking service…` immediately.\n5. After the simulated delay, observe `Sync failed` again instead of `All changes are synced.`\n\nBounded fix: Make retry force the success result while preserving the initial URL-driven error state. For example, track whether this run is a retry and set the result accordingly:\n```tsx\nconst isRetry = attempt > 0;\n...\nsetState(isRetry || requested !== 'error' ? 'success' : 'error');\n```\nor store the initial query result in a ref and let `handleRetry()` trigger a success attempt. Keep the existing effect cleanup so timers remain non-overlapping.","type":"output_text","logprobs":[]}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":"final_answer"}],"timestamp":"2026-11-22T15:57:23.505583+00:00"}],"meta":{"snapshot_version":1,"aid":1,"role":"workflow_agent","model":"deepseek-flash","session_state":{"used_tokens":2296,"context_tokens":1432,"step_count":1,"markup_recovered":0,"recent_call_hashes":[],"reads_since_last_edit":0,"has_landed_write":false,"low_yield_since_progress":0,"distinct_evidence_count":0,"scout_ledger":[],"steps_since_progress":0,"wind_down_done":false,"wind_down_attempts":0,"wind_down_token_mark":0,"budget_reserve_consumed":false,"loop_blocked_since_progress":0,"loop_state":{"version":1,"edit_seq":0,"blocked_rounds":0,"last_counted_step":-1,"operations":{}},"write_effect_unknown":false,"last_progress_unknown":false,"phase":"done","terminal_reason":"completed","pending_events":[],"pending_external_user_turn":null,"active_turn_start_message_index":null,"completed_turn_start_message_index":2,"pending_step_latency":null,"submitted_summary":null,"anthropic_history":null},"run_id":"workflow-2db77a65e5784ca5989409479ac96135"},"seen_result_hashes_reset":false,"seen_result_hashes_added":[]}
